Gap behind k261: ci.yml runs the Node build on Windows, perl.yml runs prove on Linux only (perl:5.40-bookworm container). The only Windows Perl run is the binaries probe (dzil-binary.yml, workflow_dispatch), so the k251 SIGHUP load failure reached ack-paket unseen.

Plan (main agent's call, 2026-11-19): a cheap Windows leg in perl.yml that installs the deps with the same setup the binaries workflow uses (shogo82148/actions-setup-perl, Strawberry) and loads every module (t/00-load.t plus the k261 regression test), with workflow_dispatch so it can be probed on a branch before main. The full prove on Windows has never run and is not claimed here: it goes to a backlog card.

2026-11-19 08:21 Added a load-windows job to .github/workflows/perl.yml and workflow_dispatch to its triggers; the Linux job is unchanged. Setup taken verbatim from the pinned dzil-binary.yml (c339eef) Windows leg: runs-on windows-latest, shogo82148/actions-setup-perl@v1 with perl-version 5.40 and distribution strawberry, PERL_CPANM_OPT as the Linux job. Steps run in the default shell pwsh, where setup-perl's perl comes first (the reusable workflow reads it there with Get-Command perl.exe; Git Bash would put its own perl ahead): perl -S cpanm -nq --installdeps . and perl -S prove -l t/00-load.t t/03-load-win32-signals.t (perl -S as build-leg.sh runs cpanm). Cheap and safe as far as visible: 00-load.t only use_ok's modules, all of which loaded on Windows in binaries run 44253898506; the deps are the same set the binaries' deps step installs on the same Strawberry (no TLS build needed: Strawberry's Net::SSLeay and IO::Socket::SSL satisfy the cpanfile, binary-prepare only matters for the packed binary); .gitattributes keeps LF. test/perl-ci-contract.test.ts pinned one installdeps and one checkout in perl.yml: now one per job, each the dist's, and no checkout of another repository. Validated: actionlint 1.7.12 (docker) clean, YAML parses. Not verifiable here: the job itself on a Windows runner (cpanm's install time, prove there).

